tonight the wife of the security guard  shot and killed in the wynn employee  parking garage is speaking out this is  an emotional interview  and she is asking who's to blame the  shooting happened tuesday night  police say an employee killed  31-year-old joseph almonte before  killing himself  joe moeller joins us live near where it  happened with what el monte's wife told  him  joe kirsten this is such a tragedy as  you can imagine the sadness coming from  the family of the victim and a shock and  grief coming from the family of the man  accused  and also in las vegas having something  like this happen happen here involving  their employees  security officer joseph amonte responded  to a call in the employee parking garage  where reggie tagget was  sitting in a car taggett was recently  reported missing and also a no-show from  work for two days but showed up using  his badge to get into the garage  amonte was doing a welfare check when he  pulled out a gun and shot a monte eight  times in the torso  i spoke to amante's wife at a las vegas  brazilian jiu jitsu gym where he worked  out several times a week  she tells me her husband who was a  marine told her he did not feel safe at  the resort since the brawl that took  place  in the encore lobby labor day weekend  you may remember the viral videos and  photos surfacing on social media  she says she asked her husband about  bulletproof vests after that incident  and i told him i was like what about  aves and he's like we have been  asking for like three years you know  everyone he's like everybody's scared  but  they went had neglected them because  they said  it did not look good for the guests  it was going to be intimidating for the  guests  marjorie says she met her husband in  2018 at the wynn resort where she also  used to work  almonte will be buried in new york where  he is originally from  she says wynn representatives have been  in contact with her and are helping with  funeral expenses  friends have also set up a gofundme to  help you can find a link to that  up on our website
 

